    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488-a1">

                <pb facs="0646" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg534"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 5, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to this Department’s letters of
                    June 1 and July 11 last, concerning the appeal made by the Government of Liberia
                    for a loan of $5,000,000 from the United States, I have the honor to enclose
                    herewith a copy of a despatch from the American Consulate General at
                        London,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d488-f1"/> transmitting a proposed supplemental
                    agreement between the Government of Liberia and the Bank of British <pb
                        facs="0647" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/> West Africa, which has been submitted
                    by the Bank to the British Foreign Office, to be later forwarded to the French
                    Government and the Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I send this paper to you as a further evidence of the danger of the financial
                    control or Liberia passing from the United States unless the financial relief
                    sought by Liberia is granted by this Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
